 * This API lets an authenticated user (comment author or, under special
 * permissions, a moderator/administrator) update an existing comment identified
 * by both parent postId and comment id. The system enforces that updates may
 * only be made to comments the user owns, or by authorized moderation roles,
 * with all validation constraints on content and threading.
 *
 * Request must specify the target post and comment, supplying new content
 * and/or thread associations. Invalid references or blank content produces
 * errors, with history tracking updated timestamps. On success, the new comment
 * details are returned.
 *
 * Business rules ensure audit trails and uphold moderation policies. Related
 * endpoints include comment creation, deletion, and listing under post/group
 * context.
 *
 * @param props.connection
 * @param props.postId The post to which the comment belongs.
 * @param props.id The unique identifier of the comment to update.
 * @param props.body Updated values for the comment (e.g., new content, parentId
 *   for re-threading).
 * @path /bbs/posts/:postId/comments/:id
