 *
 * This test covers the core administrator workflow of editing a discussion category's
 * details, including both the name and description. It first creates a new category
 * (to safely allow updates without risk of name duplication), then updates both fields
 * with new, non-duplicate values, and finally verifies that the changes are reflected
 * in the returned object and persistent upon subsequent retrievals.
 *
 * Steps:
 * 1. Create a new category with a unique name and description via POST /bbs/categories.
 * 2. Perform an update via PUT /bbs/categories/{id} with a different, valid name and description.
 * 3. Assert the API response reflects the new name/description and has the same id.
 * 4. (If a retrieval/list endpoint exists: Retrieve the category and assert its fields match the updated values.)
